<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIAN PM SEES CURRENCY BOARD VOTE IN EARLY JAN.</title>
<headline>BULGARIAN PM SEES CURRENCY BOARD VOTE IN EARLY JAN.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian Prime Minister Zhan Videnov said on Monday he hoped parliament could vote on introduction of a currency board regime on January 2.</p>
<p>&quot;I think by December 31 we will manage to debate and take decisions on the introduction of a currency board so parliament can approve the draft proposal on January 2,&quot; Videnov told a news conference.</p>
</text>
